{"unit_id": "OAI-PF-2023-0041", "source_version": "target", "lab_name": "OpenAI", "framework_name": "Preparedness Framework", "framework_version": "NONE", "framework_year": 2023, "section_heading": "Tracked Risk Categories", "locator": "N/A", "unit_type": "paragraph", "context_stem": "NONE", "excerpt": "Our rationale for grouping and naming these specific risk categories is informed by three considerations.", "paraphrase": "Introduces three considerations behind the category groupings.", "modal_register": "none", "stated_bar": "NONE", "duplicate_of": "NONE", "removal_candidate": false, "prior_locator": "NONE", "prior_counterpart_excerpt": "NONE", "prior_modal_register": "NONE", "prior_stated_bar": "NONE", "alignment_note": "NONE"}
{"unit_id": "OAI-PF-2023-0042", "source_version": "target", "lab_name": "OpenAI", "framework_name": "Preparedness Framework", "framework_version": "NONE", "framework_year": 2023, "section_heading": "Tracked Risk Categories", "locator": "N/A", "unit_type": "paragraph", "context_stem": "NONE", "excerpt": "First, fine-tuning or other domain-specific enhancements (e.g., tailored prompts or language model programs) may better elicit model capabilities along a particular risk category.", "paraphrase": "Fine-tuning or domain-specific enhancements may reveal greater model capabilities in a given risk category.", "modal_register": "conditional", "stated_bar": "NONE", "duplicate_of": "NONE", "removal_candidate": false, "prior_locator": "NONE", "prior_counterpart_excerpt": "NONE", "prior_modal_register": "NONE", "prior_stated_bar": "NONE", "alignment_note": "NONE"}
{"unit_id": "OAI-PF-2023-0043", "source_version": "target", "lab_name": "OpenAI", "framework_name": "Preparedness Framework", "framework_version": "NONE", "framework_year": 2023, "section_heading": "Tracked Risk Categories", "locator": "N/A", "unit_type": "paragraph", "context_stem": "NONE", "excerpt": "Our evaluations will thus include tests against these enhanced models to ensure we are testing against the \"worst case\" scenario we know of.", "paraphrase": "Evaluations will include tests on enhanced models to capture the worst-case scenario.", "modal_register": "mandatory", "stated_bar": "NONE", "duplicate_of": "NONE", "removal_candidate": false, "prior_locator": "NONE", "prior_counterpart_excerpt": "NONE", "prior_modal_register": "NONE", "prior_stated_bar": "NONE", "alignment_note": "NONE"}
{"unit_id": "OAI-PF-2023-0044", "source_version": "target", "lab_name": "OpenAI", "framework_name": "Preparedness Framework", "framework_version": "NONE", "framework_year": 2023, "section_heading": "Tracked Risk Categories", "locator": "N/A", "unit_type": "paragraph", "context_stem": "NONE", "excerpt": "Our procedural commitments are triggered when any of the tracked risk categories increase in severity, rather than only when they all increase together.", "paraphrase": "Procedural commitments trigger on any single category's severity increase, not only simultaneous increases across all categories.", "modal_register": "mandatory", "stated_bar": "NONE", "duplicate_of": "NONE", "removal_candidate": false, "prior_locator": "NONE", "prior_counterpart_excerpt": "NONE", "prior_modal_register": "NONE", "prior_stated_bar": "NONE", "alignment_note": "NONE"}
{"unit_id": "OAI-PF-2023-0045", "source_version": "target", "lab_name": "OpenAI", "framework_name": "Preparedness Framework", "framework_version": "NONE", "framework_year": 2023, "section_heading": "Tracked Risk Categories", "locator": "N/A", "unit_type": "paragraph", "context_stem": "NONE", "excerpt": "Because capability improvements across different domains do not necessarily occur at the same rate, this approach ensures we err on the side of safety.", "paraphrase": "Since domains improve at different rates, this approach favors erring on the side of safety.", "modal_register": "none", "stated_bar": "NONE", "duplicate_of": "NONE", "removal_candidate": false, "prior_locator": "NONE", "prior_counterpart_excerpt": "NONE", "prior_modal_register": "NONE", "prior_stated_bar": "NONE", "alignment_note": "NONE"}
{"unit_id": "OAI-PF-2023-0046", "source_version": "target", "lab_name": "OpenAI", "framework_name": "Preparedness Framework", "framework_version": "NONE", "framework_year": 2023, "section_heading": "Tracked Risk Categories", "locator": "N/A", "unit_type": "paragraph", "context_stem": "NONE", "excerpt": "Second, this approach enables us to leverage domain-specific talent to develop tailored suites of evaluations and monitoring solutions for each risk category.", "paraphrase": "The approach allows use of domain-specific expertise to build tailored evaluation and monitoring suites.", "modal_register": "none", "stated_bar": "NONE", "duplicate_of": "NONE", "removal_candidate": false, "prior_locator": "NONE", "prior_counterpart_excerpt": "NONE", "prior_modal_register": "NONE", "prior_stated_bar": "NONE", "alignment_note": "NONE"}
{"unit_id": "OAI-PF-2023-0047", "source_version": "target", "lab_name": "OpenAI", "framework_name": "Preparedness Framework", "framework_version": "NONE", "framework_year": 2023, "section_heading": "Tracked Risk Categories", "locator": "N/A", "unit_type": "paragraph", "context_stem": "NONE", "excerpt": "Third, this approach increases options for tailored, domain-specific mitigations, to help minimize the need for broader, more disruptive actions.", "paraphrase": "The approach increases options for targeted mitigations, reducing the need for broader disruptive actions.", "modal_register": "none", "stated_bar": "NONE", "duplicate_of": "NONE", "removal_candidate": false, "prior_locator": "NONE", "prior_counterpart_excerpt": "NONE", "prior_modal_register": "NONE", "prior_stated_bar": "NONE", "alignment_note": "NONE"}
{"unit_id": "OAI-PF-2023-0048", "source_version": "target", "lab_name": "OpenAI", "framework_name": "Preparedness Framework", "framework_version": "NONE", "framework_year": 2023, "section_heading": "Tracked Risk Categories", "locator": "N/A", "unit_type": "paragraph", "context_stem": "NONE", "excerpt": "Also, the risk categories that we are considering are not necessarily independent and are likely to interact with each other.", "paraphrase": "Risk categories are not independent and are likely to interact.", "modal_register": "none", "stated_bar": "NONE", "duplicate_of": "NONE", "removal_candidate": false, "prior_locator": "NONE", "prior_counterpart_excerpt": "NONE", "prior_modal_register": "NONE", "prior_stated_bar": "NONE", "alignment_note": "NONE"}
{"unit_id": "OAI-PF-2023-0049", "source_version": "target", "lab_name": "OpenAI", "framework_name": "Preparedness Framework", "framework_version": "NONE", "framework_year": 2023, "section_heading": "Tracked Risk Categories", "locator": "N/A", "unit_type": "paragraph", "context_stem": "NONE", "excerpt": "Decisions to group certain risks are thus motivated by operational efficiencies (as well as by the desire to have a relatively compact set of Tracked Risk Categories).", "paraphrase": "Grouping decisions are driven by operational efficiency and a preference for a compact category set.", "modal_register": "none", "stated_bar": "NONE", "duplicate_of": "NONE", "removal_candidate": false, "prior_locator": "NONE", "prior_counterpart_excerpt": "NONE", "prior_modal_register": "NONE", "prior_stated_bar": "NONE", "alignment_note": "NONE"}
{"unit_id": "OAI-PF-2023-0050", "source_version": "target", "lab_name": "OpenAI", "framework_name": "Preparedness Framework", "framework_version": "NONE", "framework_year": 2023, "section_heading": "Tracked Risk Categories", "locator": "N/A", "unit_type": "paragraph", "context_stem": "NONE", "excerpt": "As mentioned, the empirical study of catastrophic risk from frontier AI models is nascent.", "paraphrase": "Empirical study of frontier model catastrophic risk is described as nascent.", "modal_register": "none", "stated_bar": "NONE", "duplicate_of": "NONE", "removal_candidate": false, "prior_locator": "NONE", "prior_counterpart_excerpt": "NONE", "prior_modal_register": "NONE", "prior_stated_bar": "NONE", "alignment_note": "NONE"}
{"unit_id": "OAI-PF-2023-0051", "source_version": "target", "lab_name": "OpenAI", "framework_name": "Preparedness Framework", "framework_version": "NONE", "framework_year": 2023, "section_heading": "Tracked Risk Categories", "locator": "N/A", "unit_type": "paragraph", "context_stem": "NONE", "excerpt": "Our current estimates of levels and thresholds for \"medium\" through \"critical\" risk are therefore speculative and will keep being refined as informed by future research.", "paraphrase": "Current risk level thresholds are speculative and will be refined through future research.", "modal_register": "aspirational", "stated_bar": "NONE", "duplicate_of": "NONE", "removal_candidate": false, "prior_locator": "NONE", "prior_counterpart_excerpt": "NONE", "prior_modal_register": "NONE", "prior_stated_bar": "NONE", "alignment_note": "NONE"}
{"unit_id": "OAI-PF-2023-0052", "source_version": "target", "lab_name": "OpenAI", "framework_name": "Preparedness Framework", "framework_version": "NONE", "framework_year": 2023, "section_heading": "Tracked Risk Categories", "locator": "N/A", "unit_type": "paragraph", "context_stem": "NONE", "excerpt": "For this reason, we defer specific details on evaluations to the Scorecard section (and this section is intended to be updated frequently).", "paraphrase": "Specific evaluation details are deferred to the Scorecard section, which will be updated frequently.", "modal_register": "aspirational", "stated_bar": "NONE", "duplicate_of": "NONE", "removal_candidate": false, "prior_locator": "NONE", "prior_counterpart_excerpt": "NONE", "prior_modal_register": "NONE", "prior_stated_bar": "NONE", "alignment_note": "NONE"}
{"unit_id": "OAI-PF-2023-0053", "source_version": "target", "lab_name": "OpenAI", "framework_name": "Preparedness Framework", "framework_version": "NONE", "framework_year": 2023, "section_heading": "Cybersecurity", "locator": "N/A", "unit_type": "paragraph", "context_stem": "NONE", "excerpt": "Cybersecurity is focused on risks related to use of the model for cyber-exploitation to disrupt confidentiality, integrity, and/or availability of computer systems.", "paraphrase": "Cybersecurity category covers risks of the model being used to disrupt confidentiality, integrity, or availability of computer systems.", "modal_register": "none", "stated_bar": "NONE", "duplicate_of": "NONE", "removal_candidate": false, "prior_locator": "NONE", "prior_counterpart_excerpt": "NONE", "prior_modal_register": "NONE", "prior_stated_bar": "NONE", "alignment_note": "NONE"}
{"unit_id": "OAI-PF-2023-0054", "source_version": "target", "lab_name": "OpenAI", "framework_name": "Preparedness Framework", "framework_version": "NONE", "framework_year": 2023, "section_heading": "Cybersecurity", "locator": "Table Cybersecurity / Low / Definition", "unit_type": "table_cell", "context_stem": "Risk level: Low; Column: Definition", "excerpt": "Model assistance for cyberattacks, if any, is meaningful only for non-programming uses, e.g., translation, targeted distillation of confidential information, and/or data analysis AND model cannot meaningfully execute elements of cyber operations, e.g., developing a known exploit into an attack, black-box exploitation, translating reasoning about defenses into action, or lateral goal-directed movement on hardened targets.", "paraphrase": "Low cybersecurity risk means the model only meaningfully assists non-programming tasks and cannot execute cyber operation elements.", "modal_register": "none", "stated_bar": "NONE", "duplicate_of": "NONE", "removal_candidate": false, "prior_locator": "NONE", "prior_counterpart_excerpt": "NONE", "prior_modal_register": "NONE", "prior_stated_bar": "NONE", "alignment_note": "NONE"}
{"unit_id": "OAI-PF-2023-0055", "source_version": "target", "lab_name": "OpenAI", "framework_name": "Preparedness Framework", "framework_version": "NONE", "framework_year": 2023, "section_heading": "Cybersecurity", "locator": "Table Cybersecurity / Low / Rationale", "unit_type": "table_cell", "context_stem": "Risk level: Low; Column: Rationale for threshold", "excerpt": "Non-programming tasks represent a sizable bottleneck for threat actors; however, the skills involved are not terribly specialized and the benefit comes often from intersectional skills (i.e., proficiency in English and a high level understanding of political or technical systems to summarize emails).", "paraphrase": "Non-programming tasks are a bottleneck but rely on non-specialized intersectional skills.", "modal_register": "none", "stated_bar": "NONE", "duplicate_of": "NONE", "removal_candidate": false, "prior_locator": "NONE", "prior_counterpart_excerpt": "NONE", "prior_modal_register": "NONE", "prior_stated_bar": "NONE", "alignment_note": "NONE"}
{"unit_id": "OAI-PF-2023-0056", "source_version": "target", "lab_name": "OpenAI", "framework_name": "Preparedness Framework", "framework_version": "NONE", "framework_year": 2023, "section_heading": "Cybersecurity", "locator": "Table Cybersecurity / Low / Rationale", "unit_type": "table_cell", "context_stem": "Risk level: Low; Column: Rationale for threshold", "excerpt": "We exclude vulnerability discovery because the harm at this stage is not identification of individual vulnerabilities, but moreso the implementation and deployment of an exploit against a target.", "paraphrase": "Vulnerability discovery is excluded because harm arises from exploit implementation/deployment, not identification.", "modal_register": "none", "stated_bar": "NONE", "duplicate_of": "NONE", "removal_candidate": false, "prior_locator": "NONE", "prior_counterpart_excerpt": "NONE", "prior_modal_register": "NONE", "prior_stated_bar": "NONE", "alignment_note": "NONE"}
{"unit_id": "OAI-PF-2023-0057", "source_version": "target", "lab_name": "OpenAI", "framework_name": "Preparedness Framework", "framework_version": "NONE", "framework_year": 2023, "section_heading": "Cybersecurity", "locator": "Table Cybersecurity / Medium / Definition", "unit_type": "table_cell", "context_stem": "Risk level: Medium; Column: Definition", "excerpt": "Model increases the productivity of operators by an efficiency threshold (e.g. >2x time saved) on key cyber operation tasks, such as developing a known exploit into an attack, black-box exploitation, goal-directed lateral movement, identification of valuable information, remaining undetected, or reacting to defense.", "paraphrase": "Medium cybersecurity risk is defined as the model providing over 2x efficiency gains on key cyber operation tasks.", "modal_register": "none", "stated_bar": ">2x time saved", "duplicate_of": "NONE", "removal_candidate": false, "prior_locator": "NONE", "prior_counterpart_excerpt": "NONE", "prior_modal_register": "NONE", "prior_stated_bar": "NONE", "alignment_note": "NONE"}
{"unit_id": "OAI-PF-2023-0058", "source_version": "target", "lab_name": "OpenAI", "framework_name": "Preparedness Framework", "framework_version": "NONE", "framework_year": 2023, "section_heading": "Cybersecurity", "locator": "Table Cybersecurity / Medium / Rationale", "unit_type": "table_cell", "context_stem": "Risk level: Medium; Column: Rationale for threshold", "excerpt": "The execution of a cyberattack is a scarce skill that is generally learned from experience. A model's ability to substitute in for or accelerate a professional would improve the quality or quantity of attacks.", "paraphrase": "Cyberattack execution is scarce skill; models substituting for professionals could improve attack quality/quantity.", "modal_register": "none", "stated_bar": "NONE", "duplicate_of": "NONE", "removal_candidate": false, "prior_locator": "NONE", "prior_counterpart_excerpt": "NONE", "prior_modal_register": "NONE", "prior_stated_bar": "NONE", "alignment_note": "NONE"}
{"unit_id": "OAI-PF-2023-0059", "source_version": "target", "lab_name": "OpenAI", "framework_name": "Preparedness Framework", "framework_version": "NONE", "framework_year": 2023, "section_heading": "Cybersecurity", "locator": "Table Cybersecurity / Medium / Rationale", "unit_type": "table_cell", "context_stem": "Risk level: Medium; Column: Rationale for threshold", "excerpt": "Note that this productivity speedup also includes low-level (potentially state) actors using known methods, e.g. Russian disinformation groups, who use purchased capabilities, phishing, and otherwise known methods.", "paraphrase": "The productivity speedup consideration includes low-level or state actors using known attack methods.", "modal_register": "none", "stated_bar": "NONE", "duplicate_of": "NONE", "removal_candidate": false, "prior_locator": "NONE", "prior_counterpart_excerpt": "NONE", "prior_modal_register": "NONE", "prior_stated_bar": "NONE", "alignment_note": "NONE"}
{"unit_id": "OAI-PF-2023-0060", "source_version": "target", "lab_name": "OpenAI", "framework_name": "Preparedness Framework", "framework_version": "NONE", "framework_year": 2023, "section_heading": "Cybersecurity", "locator": "Table Cybersecurity / High / Definition", "unit_type": "table_cell", "context_stem": "Risk level: High; Column: Definition", "excerpt": "Tool-augmented model can identify and develop proofs-of-concept for high-value exploits against hardened targets without human intervention, potentially involving novel exploitation techniques, OR provided with a detailed strategy, the model can end-to-end execute cyber operations involving the above tasks without human intervention.", "paraphrase": "High cybersecurity risk means the model can autonomously develop high-value exploits or execute cyber operations end-to-end given a strategy.", "modal_register": "none", "stated_bar": "NONE", "duplicate_of": "NONE", "removal_candidate": false, "prior_locator": "NONE", "prior_counterpart_excerpt": "NONE", "prior_modal_register": "NONE", "prior_stated_bar": "NONE", "alignment_note": "NONE"}
{"unit_id": "OAI-PF-2023-0061", "source_version": "target", "lab_name": "OpenAI", "framework_name": "Preparedness Framework", "framework_version": "NONE", "framework_year": 2023, "section_heading": "Cybersecurity", "locator": "Table Cybersecurity / High / Rationale", "unit_type": "table_cell", "context_stem": "Risk level: High; Column: Rationale for threshold", "excerpt": "High-value exploits are generally against hardened platforms, scarce, and easily productionizable (e.g., a zero-click iOS exploit).", "paraphrase": "High-value exploits target hardened platforms, are scarce, and easily productionizable.", "modal_register": "none", "stated_bar": "NONE", "duplicate_of": "NONE", "removal_candidate": false, "prior_locator": "NONE", "prior_counterpart_excerpt": "NONE", "prior_modal_register": "NONE", "prior_stated_bar": "NONE", "alignment_note": "NONE"}
{"unit_id": "OAI-PF-2023-0062", "source_version": "target", "lab_name": "OpenAI", "framework_name": "Preparedness Framework", "framework_version": "NONE", "framework_year": 2023, "section_heading": "Cybersecurity", "locator": "Table Cybersecurity / High / Rationale", "unit_type": "table_cell", "context_stem": "Risk level: High; Column: Rationale for threshold", "excerpt": "While weaker vulnerability detection capabilities (e.g. those already cheaply available and fairly liquid on exploit markets) do not meaningfully address a bottleneck for attackers, such advanced capability would unblock many and be usable by actors of many skill levels.", "paraphrase": "Weaker vulnerability detection doesn't address the attacker bottleneck, but advanced capability would unblock many actors.", "modal_register": "none", "stated_bar": "NONE", "duplicate_of": "NONE", "removal_candidate": false, "prior_locator": "NONE", "prior_counterpart_excerpt": "NONE", "prior_modal_register": "NONE", "prior_stated_bar": "NONE", "alignment_note": "NONE"}
{"unit_id": "OAI-PF-2023-0063", "source_version": "target", "lab_name": "OpenAI", "framework_name": "Preparedness Framework", "framework_version": "NONE", "framework_year": 2023, "section_heading": "Cybersecurity", "locator": "Table Cybersecurity / High / Rationale", "unit_type": "table_cell", "context_stem": "Risk level: High; Column: Rationale for threshold", "excerpt": "End-to-end execution would dramatically accelerate the quality or quantity of professional cyberattacks.", "paraphrase": "End-to-end execution would greatly accelerate professional cyberattack quality/quantity.", "modal_register": "none", "stated_bar": "NONE", "duplicate_of": "NONE", "removal_candidate": false, "prior_locator": "NONE", "prior_counterpart_excerpt": "NONE", "prior_modal_register": "NONE", "prior_stated_bar": "NONE", "alignment_note": "NONE"}
{"unit_id": "OAI-PF-2023-0064", "source_version": "target", "lab_name": "OpenAI", "framework_name": "Preparedness Framework", "framework_version": "NONE", "framework_year": 2023, "section_heading": "Cybersecurity", "locator": "Table Cybersecurity / Critical / Definition", "unit_type": "table_cell", "context_stem": "Risk level: Critical; Column: Definition", "excerpt": "Tool-augmented model can identify and develop functional zero-day exploits of all severity levels, across all software projects, without human intervention OR model can devise and execute end-to-end novel strategies for cyberattacks against hardened targets given only a high level desired goal.", "paraphrase": "Critical cybersecurity risk means the model can autonomously develop zero-day exploits across all software or execute novel cyberattack strategies given only a high-level goal.", "modal_register": "none", "stated_bar": "NONE", "duplicate_of": "NONE", "removal_candidate": false, "prior_locator": "NONE", "prior_counterpart_excerpt": "NONE", "prior_modal_register": "NONE", "prior_stated_bar": "NONE", "alignment_note": "NONE"}
{"unit_id": "OAI-PF-2023-0065", "source_version": "target", "lab_name": "OpenAI", "framework_name": "Preparedness Framework", "framework_version": "NONE", "framework_year": 2023, "section_heading": "Cybersecurity", "locator": "Table Cybersecurity / Critical / Rationale", "unit_type": "table_cell", "context_stem": "Risk level: Critical; Column: Rationale for threshold", "excerpt": "Finding and executing end-to-end exploits for all software would lead to catastrophe from unilateral actors, from hacking military or industrial systems as well as OpenAI infrastructure.", "paraphrase": "End-to-end exploits for all software could cause catastrophe via unilateral actors hacking military, industrial, or OpenAI systems.", "modal_register": "none", "stated_bar": "NONE", "duplicate_of": "NONE", "removal_candidate": false, "prior_locator": "NONE", "prior_counterpart_excerpt": "NONE", "prior_modal_register": "NONE", "prior_stated_bar": "NONE", "alignment_note": "NONE"}
{"unit_id": "OAI-PF-2023-0066", "source_version": "target", "lab_name": "OpenAI", "framework_name": "Preparedness Framework", "framework_version": "NONE", "framework_year": 2023, "section_heading": "Cybersecurity", "locator": "Table Cybersecurity / Critical / Rationale", "unit_type": "table_cell", "context_stem": "Risk level: Critical; Column: Rationale for threshold", "excerpt": "Novel cyber operations generally pose the most serious threat, as they are unpredictable and scarce. They may involve, e.g., novel zero-days or methods of command-and-control.", "paraphrase": "Novel cyber operations are the most serious threat due to unpredictability and scarcity.", "modal_register": "none", "stated_bar": "NONE", "duplicate_of": "NONE", "removal_candidate": false, "prior_locator": "NONE", "prior_counterpart_excerpt": "NONE", "prior_modal_register": "NONE", "prior_stated_bar": "NONE", "alignment_note": "NONE"}
